---
title: Upgrading to 4.2.0
description: API changes and stricter configuration conversion in Yacla 4.2.0.
---

## Update dependencies together

Use `4.2.0` for core and all selected format modules, and recompile consumers against the new API.

## Removed registry

`UpdateStrategyRegistry` has been removed. Replace global registrations with a parser's `defaultUpdateStrategy`, builder `updateStrategy(...)`, or shared `LoaderSettings.updateStrategy`.

Builder `updateStrategy(null)` explicitly disables updates. A null strategy in shared settings uses the parser's default instead.

## Custom parsers and builders

- Custom parsers must return `Map<String, Any?>` from `parse(...)`.
- Implement `write(OutputStream, Map<String, Any?>)` and leave caller-owned streams open.
- Replace direct object writing with document maps.
- Custom `ConfigLoaderBuilder` implementations must implement `updateStrategy(UpdateStrategy?)`.

## JSON dependency

The JSON module no longer depends on Jackson's Kotlin module: parsing works on document maps. Applications using that transitive dependency for their own Jackson object mapping must declare it themselves.

## Fix invalid configurations

Present invalid values no longer silently use defaults. Unknown enum elements are rejected instead of skipped. Explicit null for a non-null field fails even when a default exists. Integer fractions, overflow, non-finite floats, invalid booleans, and invalid collection elements cause conversion errors.

Review [mapping and validation](/yacla/mapping/) and correct affected files before loading them.

## File compatibility

YAML and JSON file formats remain supported. No data-format migration is required. Existing `Yacla.yaml`, `Yacla.json`, builder entry points, and language selection methods remain available. The stricter validation rules can still require edits to previously accepted invalid values.
